---
// Timeoff — COSIGN (Patient Portal) case study. Shares the stripped project system
// (painterly /work backdrop, no mat, one plain left-hung column, red as a whisper, Inter),
// ONE BEAT PER SCREEN. Demos are self-hosted local .mp4 (like cove-landing), native
// 1672×1080, autoplaying only while in view. Auto-cycling reference deck (JPL-style) uses
// square cards to suit the portrait/square Karl & Faber artwork.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ref1 from '../assets/cosign-ref-1.jpeg';
import ref2 from '../assets/cosign-ref-2.jpeg';
import ref3 from '../assets/cosign-ref-3.jpeg';
import ref4 from '../assets/cosign-ref-4.jpeg';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>COSIGN — Timeoff</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400..800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script is:inline>
      // Paint the mobile theme from the first frame: stamp <html> before <body> renders,
      // so there's no flash of the desktop (red text / textured bg) on navigation.
      if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(max-width: 768px)').matches) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('is-mobile');
      }
    </script>
    <script is:inline>
      if (sessionStorage.getItem('navTL')) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('pre-tl');
        sessionStorage.removeItem('navTL');
      }
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="page">
      <!-- ——— hero ——— -->
      <section class="panel hero-panel">
        <header class="hero">
          <p class="kicker reveal">Product Design · Front End · 2026</p>
          <h1 class="title reveal">COSIGN</h1>
          <p class="subtitle reveal">Patient Portal</p>
          <p class="scroll-hint reveal">Scroll ↓</p>
        </header>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— intro ——— -->
      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>Cosign was another product of an interview process &mdash; I thought this project would be a breeze, but boy was I wrong. The brief was to design a patient chart portal for a family clinic&hellip; and that&rsquo;s about the only simple thing about it. Extra requirements included things such as the following:</p>
          <ul class="brief">
            <li>Accommodate two views and levels of access, but keep the chart the same (physician and PA)</li>
            <li>Decide how the relevant data to today&rsquo;s visit becomes visible with a quick scan
              <ul>
                <li>Without hiding the rest of the chart data</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Decide how the PA views restricted content, and how they request access
              <ul>
                <li>Access is limited time and expires. Design how this works and shows up visually on both ends</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Build a notes system so the PA can draft notes and the physician can co-sign them (hence the name)
              <ul>
                <li>Notes must have a lifecycle (Draft, Submitted, and Co-Signed or Returned with Comments)</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>And finally&hellip; an Audit view only the physician can see</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Regardless, I was tested and forced to learn and adapt, which is always good. This one came together in roughly 5 days.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— 1 · main screen ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The main screen..</p>
          <div class="video-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio: 1672 / 1080;">
            <video class="local-demo" src="/cosign-main.mp4" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>Here is the main view, the patient chart for Jordan Reyes, who I hope is fictional&hellip;</p>
          <p>Anyways, I had never designed anything like this before. Beyond that, I didn&rsquo;t just have to make it look pretty, I had to make it function just as good. I started out by wasting a full day trying to just design a patient chart from scratch, using my web design skills and intuition, trying to make things look cool, etc. Nothing worked. I kept ending up with ugly charts that looked like they came from a 1980&rsquo;s medicine textbook.</p>
          <p>So I decided to go a different route. I was going to design this thing brick by brick. Make the small parts look pretty and work well, and then build the whole thing piece by piece, slot things together and see how they look and feel &mdash; and that was the key for building this project.</p>
          <p>I started with the data cards, then I designed the rows and the little visual effects, and then I just kept piling on things little by little until eventually I had really good &ldquo;pieces&rdquo; to put together.</p>
          <p>I tried not to look at too many patient chart references because I thought it would be fun to try and do this from an outsider&rsquo;s perspective. I actually leaned heavily on a weird mixture of references and styles: One being Google&rsquo;s general styling, and then I found this art auction house who had a really cool art and marketing style that I pulled a lot of the type and font choices from.</p>
          <p>I was left with this type-forward, bento style grid that simply just worked well. Sometimes you have to shift energy from making the coolest looking thing that functions okay, and reverse that way of thinking. Here we have something that works great and looks to me&hellip; pretty good. If I was a physician, this is the patient chart I&rsquo;d want to use.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— 2 · two-up view ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">Two trust levels..</p>
          <div class="video-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio: 1672 / 1080;">
            <video class="local-demo" src="/cosign-two-view.mp4" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>This is a quick demo of how I implemented this &ldquo;two view / two levels of access&rdquo; solution. I made strong use of these &ldquo;footers&rdquo; on the row(s) because they didn&rsquo;t technically change the chart, but they added the context and functionality I needed.</p>
          <p>The other things to consider were the audit function, the restricted access, and the confidential note. You will see how they function next&hellip;</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— 3 · access ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">Access & permissions..</p>
          <div class="video-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio: 1672 / 1080;">
            <video class="local-demo" src="/cosign-access.mp4" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>Now some of the fun stuff&hellip; the aforementioned restricted access. I decided the PA could see that there was a restricted result because maybe he would want to request it to give proper care. As for the confidential note, I decided that was only for the physician to see.</p>
          <p>These were sort of easy to decide and design conceptually, PA can&rsquo;t see, requests access, physician grants timed access that they both can see&hellip; whatever. But let me tell you, once that first layer is built and you run through it, you notice a new issue every time&hellip; most of the time they are small things, but that&rsquo;s what drives you nuts.</p>
          <p>Okay the main function is there, but how should the dropdown look? It should have a timestamp, shouldn&rsquo;t it? What gets put into the pill/button shape? What doesn&rsquo;t? How do we notify? Etc.</p>
          <p>That theme carried on into multiple areas of the project, partially because of my OCD, partially because design is a granular thing. In the end we landed on a smooth interaction.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— 4 · notes & audit ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">Notes & the audit trail..</p>
          <div class="video-wrapper" style="aspect-ratio: 1672 / 1080;">
            <video class="local-demo" src="/cosign-notes.mp4" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>Now for the notes and audit duo&hellip; thankfully these were the last things I built, so I had already built up an almost fully designed system for them to slot into. I decided to make them both live on the bottom corners, which I feel is a good home for them. They wouldn&rsquo;t look good in the patient info header, and they don&rsquo;t belong in the main header (designed to be a part of a larger, assumed EHR) because they are patient specific.</p>
          <p>The notes flow was pretty simple to conceptualize, as well as the audit. Notes gets a few handoffs and a lifecycle, along with a physician only confidential note &mdash; and then the audit tab is&hellip; well&hellip; just an audit tab with a few more features.</p>
          <p>As I mentioned before, these are seemingly simple, but even when they were 90% done, I spent more time fine tuning the last 10% than I did building the initial 90%&hellip; story of my life.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— closing: wrap-up + visit the live site ——— -->
      <section class="panel closing-panel">
        <div class="closing">
          <div class="text reveal">
            <p>And there you have it! A nice, modern, and kinda cool looking patient chart portal. This was one of the more challenging, yet most rewarding projects I&rsquo;ve done. I can&rsquo;t emphasize enough HOW MUCH EFFORT WENT INTO THE FINE TUNING. Whether it was visual or functional. I would get it to like 80-90% and then spend double the time working out the small details. But, that&rsquo;s the name of the game.</p>
            <p>I really enjoyed working on this one, poke around in the live site &mdash; there&rsquo;s plenty of little things I couldn&rsquo;t cover in the demos or this write up.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="closing-row reveal">
            <div class="deck">
              <p class="caption">Art auction house references..</p>
              <div class="stack">
                <div class="stack-card stack-card-1"><Image src={ref1} alt="Karl & Faber — a portrait of a woman in a red dress under the KARL&FABER wordmark" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="440px" loading="lazy" /></div>
                <div class="stack-card stack-card-2"><Image src={ref2} alt="Two Karl & Faber auction catalogs resting on a stone ledge" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="440px" loading="lazy" /></div>
                <div class="stack-card stack-card-3"><Image src={ref3} alt="Karl & Faber — an oil painting of a horseman with the tagline Search. Bid. Collect." widths={[480, 960]} sizes="440px" loading="lazy" /></div>
                <div class="stack-card stack-card-4"><Image src={ref4} alt="The Karl & Faber auction house homepage" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="440px" loading="lazy" /></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="visit-block">
              <img class="visit-note" src="/click_to_visit_trim.png" alt="Click to visit the site" width="340" height="64" />
              <a class="omnibox" href="https://cosign-two.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the live COSIGN patient portal at cosign-two.vercel.app">
                <svg class="omnibox-lock" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor"><path d="M11 7V5a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v2H4v7h8V7h-1zm-4-2a1 1 0 0 1 2 0v2H7V5z"/></svg>
                <span class="omnibox-url">cosign-two.vercel.app</span>
                <svg class="omnibox-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— next project ——— -->
      <section class="panel next-panel">
        <a class="next reveal" href="/bird-dog">
          <span class="next-kicker">Next</span>
          <span class="next-title">Bird Dog</span>
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <nav class="chrome" aria-label="site">
      <a class="label tl work grow" href="/work">Work</a>
      <a class="label tr info grow" href="/information">Information</a>
    </nav>

    <style>
      :root {
        --fg: #d6352a;                       /* red — accent (kicker, title) */
        --ink: #26241f;                      /* warm near-black — body reading ink */
        --muted: rgba(38, 36, 31, 0.5);      /* captions */
      }
      * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { background: #eef0ec; scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body {
        /* painterly backdrop, kept as-is — content sits straight on the painting, no mat */
        background: #eef0ec url('/work-bg.png') center / cover no-repeat fixed;
        color: var(--ink);
        font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        min-height: 100vh;
      }

      /* ——— the column: one plain centered measure; painting shows in the gutters ——— */
      .page {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        max-width: min(92vw, 1080px);
        margin: 0 auto;
        animation: page-in 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) backwards;
        transition: opacity 0.3s ease-out;
      }
      @keyframes page-in {
        from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
        to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
      }
      .page.leaving { opacity: 0; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .page { animation: none; }
        .page.leaving { opacity: 1; transition: none; }
      }

      /* ——— one beat per screen, everything hung to the same left edge ——— */
      .panel {
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: grid;
        align-content: center;
        justify-items: start;
        padding: 12vh 0;
      }

      /* ——— hero ——— */
      .hero { text-align: left; }
      .kicker { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fg); margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
      .title { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); }
      .subtitle { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); margin-top: 0.2rem; }
      .scroll-hint { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 3.5rem; }

      /* ——— bare media — no frame, no shadow, demos all at 1060px ——— */
      .media { max-width: 1060px; width: 100%; }
      .caption { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.01em; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
      .media .video-wrapper { display: block; }
      .video-wrapper { position: relative; width: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #ddd; }
      .video-wrapper video { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }

      /* ——— text: quiet, left-hung, one calm treatment (ref: Studio Small) ——— */
      .text-panel p {
        max-width: 58ch;
        font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.35vw, 1.16rem);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: var(--ink);
      }
      .text { max-width: 58ch; }
      .text p { max-width: none; }
      .text p + p { margin-top: 1.4rem; }
      /* placeholder copy — obvious at a glance, to be replaced */
      .placeholder { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }

      /* ——— brief list — quiet, red dash markers, nested items demoted ——— */
      .text ul { list-style: none; margin: 1.4rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
      .text ul + p { margin-top: 1.4rem; }
      .text li {
        position: relative;
        padding-left: 1.5rem;
        margin-top: 0.7rem;
        font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.35vw, 1.16rem);
        line-height: 1.7;
      }
      .text li::before { content: '—'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--fg); }
      .text li ul { margin: 0.55rem 0 0.2rem; }
      .text li li { color: var(--muted); }
      .text li li::before { content: '+'; color: var(--muted); }

      /* ——— reveal-on-scroll: rises into frame, weighted easing ——— */
      .reveal {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(40px);
        transition: opacity 1s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), transform 1s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
        will-change: opacity, transform;
      }
      .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none; }
      }

      /* ——— art auction house reference deck: auto-cycling card stack (ref: JPL) ——— */
      .deck { flex: 0 0 auto; }
      .stack { position: relative; margin-top: 1.2rem; width: clamp(240px, 30vw, 400px); aspect-ratio: 1 / 1; }
      .stack-card { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1 / 1; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0,0,0,0.2); will-change: transform, opacity; }
      .stack-card :global(img) { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
      .stack-card-1 { z-index: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(-16px, 14px) rotate(-7deg); }
      .stack-card-2 { z-index: 2; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(12px, 8px) rotate(5deg); animation: stack2 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }
      .stack-card-3 { z-index: 3; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(-6px, 0) rotate(-3deg); animation: stack3 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }
      .stack-card-4 { z-index: 4; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(8px, -8px) rotate(2deg); animation: stack4 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }
      @keyframes stack2 { 0%, 8% { opacity: 0; } 9%, 100% { opacity: 1; } }
      @keyframes stack3 { 0%, 38% { opacity: 0; } 39%, 100% { opacity: 1; } }
      @keyframes stack4 { 0%, 68% { opacity: 0; } 69%, 100% { opacity: 1; } }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .stack-card { animation: none; opacity: 1; } }

      /* ——— closing: wrap-up + visit the live site ——— */
      .closing-panel { min-height: 100vh; }
      .closing { width: 100%; max-width: 980px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2.6rem; }
      .closing-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 3.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .visit-block { flex: 1 1 260px; max-width: 340px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
      .visit-note { display: block; width: 300px; max-width: 100%; height: auto; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0 0 0.9rem 0.5rem; pointer-events: none; }
      .omnibox { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 18px; background: #f1f3f4; border: 1px solid #e4e6e8; border-radius: 999px; text-decoration: none; overflow: hidden; transition: background 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, transform 0.25s ease; }
      .omnibox:hover { background: #eceef0; box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); transform: translateY(-1px); }
      .omnibox-lock { width: 13px; height: 13px; color: #5f6368; flex-shrink: 0; }
      .omnibox-url { flex: 1; font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #202124; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
      .omnibox-arrow { width: 16px; height: 16px; color: #5f6368; flex-shrink: 0; transition: transform 0.25s ease, color 0.25s ease; }
      .omnibox:hover .omnibox-arrow { transform: translateX(4px); color: #202124; }
      .omnibox::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: -60%; width: 55%; height: 100%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255,255,255,0.75), transparent); transform: skewX(-20deg); pointer-events: none; }
      .omnibox:hover::after { animation: omnibox-shimmer 0.9s ease; }
      @keyframes omnibox-shimmer { from { left: -60%; } to { left: 130%; } }

      /* ——— next project ——— */
      .next-panel { min-height: 70vh; }
      .next { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; text-decoration: none; }
      .next-kicker { font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
      .next-title { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); transition: transform 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
      .next:hover .next-title { transform: translateX(0.6rem); }

      /* ——— corner chrome (matches /work) ——— */
      .chrome { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 4; pointer-events: none; mix-blend-mode: difference; }
      .label { position: fixed; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff; }
      .grow { pointer-events: auto; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1; will-change: font-size; transition: font-size 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), letter-spacing 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), font-weight 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
      .grow:hover { font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .work:hover { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5.6rem); }
      .info:hover { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3.9rem); }
      html.pre-tl .grow { transition: none; }
      html.pre-tl .work { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5.6rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .tl { top: 1.9rem; left: 2.2rem; }
      .tr { top: 1.9rem; right: 2.2rem; }
      /* First-paint mobile theme (html.is-mobile set by the head script): kill the desktop
         red text + textured background on the very first frame, before the @media rules
         resolve — this is what removes the flash on navigation. */
      html.is-mobile { --fg: #141414; }
      html.is-mobile, html.is-mobile body { background: #fff; }

      /* ——— Mobile: white/black StudioSmall retheme + natural stacked scroll
         (shared project-page format; see jpl-redesign) ——— */
      @media (max-width: 768px) {
        :root { --fg: #141414; --ink: #1a1a1a; --muted: rgba(20, 20, 20, 0.46); }
        html { background: #fff; }
        body { background: #fff; overflow-x: hidden; }
        .page { max-width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0 1rem; }
        .panel { min-height: auto; padding: 4.5vh 0; }
        .hero-panel { min-height: 74vh; padding-top: 20vh; }
        .next-panel { min-height: auto; padding: 6vh 0 12vh; }
        .title, .subtitle { font-size: clamp(2rem, 8.5vw, 2.5rem); }
        .kicker { color: var(--muted); }
        .scroll-hint { margin-top: 2.4rem; }
        .media { max-width: 100%; }
        /* closing: reference deck stacks above the visit link */
        .closing-row { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 2rem; }
        .stack { width: min(72vw, 300px); }
      }
      /* Touch devices have no hover, so the nav enlarge — both the :hover growth and
         the persisted cross-page handoff (pre-tl/pre-tr) — only reads as a broken
         giant word. Keep the nav labels small and static on mobile. */
      @media (hover: none) {
        .grow, .grow:hover, html.pre-tl .grow, html.pre-tr .grow {
          font-size: 0.72rem !important;
          font-weight: 600 !important;
          letter-spacing: 0.16em !important;
        }
      }

    </style>

    <script>
      window.addEventListener('pointermove', () => {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove('pre-tl');
      }, { once: true });

      // ——— smooth exit: gentle opacity dip, then navigate (internal links only) ———
      const page = document.querySelector('.page');
      const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const a = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('a');
        if (!a) return;
        const href = a.getAttribute('href');
        if (!href || a.target === '_blank' || a.hasAttribute('download')) return;
        if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.shiftKey || e.altKey || (e as MouseEvent).button !== 0) return;
        const url = new URL(href, location.href);
        if (url.origin !== location.origin || url.pathname === location.pathname) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        if (a.classList.contains('work')) sessionStorage.setItem('navTL', '1');
        if (a.classList.contains('info')) sessionStorage.setItem('navTR', '1');
        if (reduceMotion) { window.location.href = url.href; return; }
        page?.classList.add('leaving');
        setTimeout(() => { window.location.href = url.href; }, 200);
      });
      window.addEventListener('pageshow', (e) => { if (e.persisted) page?.classList.remove('leaving'); });

      // ——— reveal-on-scroll ———
      const reveals = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
      if (reduceMotion) {
        reveals.forEach((el) => el.classList.add('in'));
      } else {
        const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          entries.forEach((en) => {
            if (en.isIntersecting) { en.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(en.target); }
          });
        }, { threshold: 0.2, rootMargin: '0px 0px -12% 0px' });
        reveals.forEach((el) => io.observe(el));
      }

      // ——— self-hosted demos: muted, play only while in view ———
      function initLocalDemos() {
        const vids = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLVideoElement>('.local-demo');
        if (!vids.length) return;
        const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          entries.forEach((en) => {
            const v = en.target as HTMLVideoElement;
            if (en.isIntersecting) {
              v.play().catch(() => {});
            } else {
              v.pause();
              v.currentTime = 0;
            }
          });
        }, { threshold: 0.5 });
        vids.forEach((v) => io.observe(v));
      }
      requestAnimationFrame(() => initLocalDemos());
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
